8. Read, not copied
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Written here after reading these, so that nobody has to guess where a
   number came from. None of their code is in this repository.

     - Linux drivers/bluetooth/btrtl.c, btbcm.c, btusb.c and
       drivers/hid/hid-nvidia-shield.c (GPL-2.0): the Realtek firmware format
       and download, vendor opcodes, a reset delay, and HID usage numbers.
       The table of ROM identifiers in portall_bt.cpp lists the values
       Realtek chips report about themselves, reproduced as data.
     - bluepad32's uni_hid_parser_android.c (Apache-2.0, Ricardo Quesada):
       Android's button numbering convention, which keys.cpp follows.
     - The USB HID 1.11 specification and the Bluetooth Core Specification's
       assigned numbers.
     - CherryUSB (Apache-2.0) is downloaded at build time, not vendored;
       cherryusb_patch changes one constant in that downloaded copy.
     - ESP-IDF's USB Host Library (Apache-2.0, Espressif), which the
       optional `transport: idf` calls instead of CherryUSB, is part of
       ESP-IDF 5.5 or downloaded as espressif/usb on ESP-IDF 6, not
       vendored. The layer over it, idf_usb.h and idf_usb.cpp in
       portall_bt and usb_bluetooth, is this repository's own, under MIT.

