9. Stand-in headers for the tests
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
   tools/btstub/ and tools/pipetest/stub/ let the C++ be compiled and run on
   a workstation. Their declarations follow ESP-IDF v5.5.5 (Apache-2.0) and
   ESPHome (C++ under GPLv3) closely enough to compile against, and keep
   their origins' licences; they are not part of any firmware.

   tools/btstub/usb/ is ESP-IDF v5.5.5's USB Host Library declarations
   (components/usb/include/usb/, Apache-2.0, Espressif), copied as they are
   there for what portall_bt's own USB layer calls. tools/idfusbtest/
   fakehost.cpp carries ESP-IDF's usb_parse_next_descriptor() as it is in
   components/usb/usb_helpers.c (Apache-2.0), and says so in its header.
   Neither is part of any firmware: on a board the library is ESP-IDF's.
